<title>DUBAI: Sharjah air cargo up 19 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Sharjah air cargo up 19 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sharjah airport said 1996 cargo volumes rose 19 percent to 320,607 tonnes from 269,067 tonnes</p>
<p>Sea-air freight exports from the emirate, the third largest member of the United Arab Emirates, rose almost 50 percent to 32,078 tonnes.</p>
<p>December cargo increased 18.7 percent to 31,297 tonnes against the same period 1995.</p>
<p>956,952 passengers passed through Sharjah airport's turnstyles from 888,129 the year before.</p>
<p>Sea-air freight exports in the month were 2,488 tonnes, more than double the 1,233 tonnes exported in December 1995. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
